          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q3",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q3",
          "passage": "Some robots such as Surena (developed in 2008)\nand COMAN (developed in 2012) feature\nhumanoid characteristics like bipedal locomotion\nso that people will find it easier to interact with\nthem. While these features can help to\n______________ feelings of comfort in\npeople, a robot that looks too like human can\nfall into the 'uncanny valley,' meaning that its\nappearance unintentionally unsettles those who\nencounter it.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "engender",
            "constrict",
            "counterbalance",
            "repudiate"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is A (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q3). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q004",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q4",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q4",
          "passage": "Text corpora such as the International Corpus of\nEnglish are enormous collections of\nelectronically stored texts that can be used for\nempirical testing of hypotheses regarding how\n_____________ a word is in spoken and\nwritten English. For instance, one might have a\nguess about the incidence of the word 'first,' but\nonly an analysis of a corpus can prove that 'first'\nis the third most commonly used adjective.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "pervasive",
            "credible",
            "assertive",
            "profound"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is A (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q4). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q005",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q5",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q5",
          "passage": "Initially, upon entering the United States in the\n1900s, the majority of European immigrants had\na lower education level than the U.S. average.\nHowever, surveys ______________ from\n1940–2017, show that European immigrants\nadvanced further in their education by the third\ngeneration than United States born whites.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "managed",
            "administered",
            "delivered",
            "supplied"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is B (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q5). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q006",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q6",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q6",
          "passage": "To avoid conflict with incoming Europeans\nattempting to colonize North America, the\nCherokee nation\n__________________ many of the\nsettler's culture, including language, religion,\nand economics. Despite this, when gold was\ndiscovered in their territory, the Indian Removal\nAct was passed in 1830 to remove the tribe from\ntheir lands and gain access to their resources.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "learned",
            "mimicked",
            "adopted",
            "rejected"
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is C (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q6). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q007",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q7",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q7",
          "passage": "Although the knowledge of the Pleistocene\nepoch and the lives of the hominids during this\ntime was once ____________, recent\nanalyses of fossils like that of the individual\nknown as Misliya -1, discovered in Israel in 2002,\nhave sharpened our picture of what a day in the\nlife of Misliya-1 may have looked like.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "intricate",
            "unprecedented",
            "concrete",
            "nebulous"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is D (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q7). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q008",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q8",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q8",
          "passage": "Whether the reign of a French monarchs such as\nLouis Philippe I or Philip II was considered\nhistorically significant or, conversely, relatively\n____________, its trajectory was shaped\nby question of legitimacy and therefore cannot\nbe understood without a corollary understanding\nof the factors that allowed the monarch to assert\na claim to the throne successfully.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "benevolent",
            "momentous",
            "inconsequential",
            "genuine"
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is C (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q8). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q009",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q9",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q9",
          "passage": "The A2X Markets in Johannesburg, South\nAfrica, connects companies operating in South\nAfrica with potential investors. This is a\nvaluable service since the time and expense\nnecessary to find individual investors might\notherwise be ____________ for these\ncompanies: many of the companies could not\noperate if they had to do everything necessary\nto find investors for themselves.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "misconstrued",
            "distinctive",
            "prohibitive",
            "beneficial"
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is C (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q9). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q010",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q10",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q10",
          "passage": "Indigenous Photograph is an organization whose\nmission is to ensure that images of Indigenous\npeoples in the media are presented from\nIndigenous perspectives. The Organization\n____________ this commitment by\npromoting the works of artist Geremew Tigabu\n(Ethiopian. Ambara, and Tigre) and other\nprominent Indigenous photographers who\ndocument and reflect indigenous lives and\nexperiences.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "concludes",
            "explains",
            "precedes",
            "shows"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is D (Answer Key: Topic 12, Q10). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t12-q011",
          "skill": "Words in Context - Gap Filling",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Select the most logical and precise word or phrase to complete the context",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 12 · Q11",
          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q11",
          "passage": "Although fewer companies trade their stocks on\nthe Cambodia Securities Exchange in Phnom\nPenh, Cambodia, than on the stock exchanges\nin London, Mumbai, or Tokyo, the Cambodia\nSecurities Exchange has the advantage of being\nable to ____________ relatively small\ncompanies in Cambodia: by connecting those\ncompanies to investors with expertise about the\ncountry's economic conditions, the Cambodia\nSecurities Exchange can help those companies\nthrive.",
          "prompt": "Which choice completes the text with the most\nlogical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": [
            "designate",
            "nurture",
            "preclude",
            "assess"
