          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q21",
          "passage": "Text corpora such as the British National\nCorpus are enormous collections of electronically\nstored texts that can be used for empirical\ntesting of hypotheses regarding how\n______________ a word is in spoken\nand written English. For instance, one might\nhave a guess about the incidence of the word\n'world,' but only an analysis of a corpus can\nprove that 'world' is the eighth most commonly\nused noun.",
