          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q26",
          "passage": "Writer Lydia Davis observed that while\ntraditional literary forms, such as the novel, are\nrecognizable as such even as they evolve, there\nare rarer 'intergeneric' forms that might, for\nexample, use elements of both fiction and essays\nto create something ______________.\nThe late-period pieces of James Tate arguably\nfit this description, since they straddle the line\nbetween prose and poetry.",
