          "passage": "Karam Kang has demonstrated that lobbying\ndoes little to alter probability that a particular\nenergy policy under consideration by the United\nStates Congress will be enacted, but lobbying is\nnot as ______________ finding seems to\nsuggest. As Kang herself notes, lobbying can\nshape which policy proposals members of\nCongress bring forward for consideration in the\nfirst place.",
