          "passage": "Postcranial skeletal pneumaticity (PSP) refers\nto the presence of extensions of an animal' s\nlungs and air sacs inside its bones. Though such\nstructures do not typically fossilize, they are\nbelieved to have been present inTyrannosaurus,\nEuhelopus, and other Cretaceous theropods and\nsauropods. To ______________ PSP\nfrom fossils, researchers look for indicators such\nas large foramina (holes in bones).",
