          "passageTitle": "Words in Context - Gap Filling — Q183",
          "passage": "Demosthenes, a prominent fourth-century BCE\nAthenian orator, is said to have been\n______________ ofparrhesia, or\nspeaking freely and openly to ensure productive\ncivic deliberation. He is noted for characterizing\nparrhesia in several public addresses as the\nfoundation of democracy in classical Athens\nrather than, more simply, as a facilitator of the\npolitical system.",
