          "passage": "Studying wrappers from discontinued candies,\nmenus from nineteenth-century restaurants, and\nflyers promoting long-forgotten sporting events\nmay seem like a frivolous pursuit, but ephemeral\nobjects like these are useful as markers of\ncultural change: they can\n______________ shifts in norms, values,\nand concerns that traditional objects of\nhistorical inquiry may not.",
