          "passage": "During the 2007-2010 financial crisis, the United\nStates furnished billions of dollars to selected\ncountries' central banks via mechanisms called\nswap lines. Aditi Sahasrabuddhe found that\ncountries' policy environments seem to have\nbeen ________ swap-line decisions: the\nprobability that banks could be granted swap\nlines was 0.20 in countries open to\nforeign-capital inflows and 0.03 in countries with\npolicies restricting such inflows.",
