          "passage": "Andrei Tarkovsky'sSolaris has the measured\npace typical of slow-cinema films. Thai\nslow-cinema director Apichatpong\nWeerasethakul(Uncle Boonmee Who Can Recall\nHis Past Lives)even states that his own work\ninduces sleep in audiences. This might suggest\nhis films are boring, but boredom does not\nalways cause sleep: boredom creates an anxious\ntension in the absence of a place to fix attention,\nand thus induces not somnolence but\n_______",
